/*
# OverlayStrata

**Internal.** The App's overlay layers — `overlays`, then `notice` — made by the first
`Floating` that opens and kept above everything else the App holds. Menus, popovers,
dialogs and sheets share the first, in the order they open (a menu opened from a dialog
paints above the dialog); toasts paint in the second, above them all. It keeps the open
overlays in the order they opened, so Esc knows which is on top. Not written in a program.

## width
The window's width when the layers are the App's (or the App's, where it is narrower);
a window's own, inside one.

## height
The window's height when the layers are the App's (or the App's, where it is shorter), so
an App that is a whole scrolling page still opens its sheets and dialogs on screen; a
window's own, inside one; the App's, where there is no window (headless).

## _isOverlayStrata
**Internal.** The marker a `Floating` finds the layers by.

## stack
The open overlays, oldest first.

## handled
The last key event an overlay acted on — so one Esc closes one overlay, however many hear it.

## opened()
Puts an overlay on top of the stack.

## closedIt()
Takes an overlay off the stack.

## top()
The open overlay the keyboard goes to — the one Esc closes — or null: the latest that
took the keys and still holds them (`Keys._claimant()`). A toast, which takes nothing, is
never it; nor is a dialog open in one window while focus is in another.
*/

class OverlayStrata [ ignoreLayout = true,
    // fixed to the App's viewport, not its content: a dialog opened with the
    // page scrolled down is on screen, and focus inside it scrolls nothing

    ignoreScroll = true,

    // the App's layers are the window's size, not the App's: an App that is the
    // page, as tall as what it holds, opens a sheet at the window's foot, not the
    // page's. A window's layers are the window's.

    width = { this.parent == app && app.hostWidth > 0 ? Math.min(app.width, app.hostWidth) : (this.parent as View).width },
    height = { this.parent == app && app.hostHeight > 0 ? Math.min(app.height, app.hostHeight) : (this.parent as View).height },

    // the layers are transparent to the pointer: what paints in them decides

    pointerEvents = "none",
    _isOverlayStrata: boolean = true,
    stack: array = [],
    handled: object = null,

    opened(v: View) { stack = stack.filter((s) => s != v).concat([v]) },
    closedIt(v: View) { stack = stack.filter((s) => s != v) },

    // the open overlay the keyboard goes to: the latest claim that holds

    top() -> View? {
        const c = Keys._claimant()
        return (stack.indexOf(c) >= 0 ? c : null) as View | null
        },

    overlays: View [ width = 100%, height = 100%, pointerEvents = "none" ],
    notice: View [ width = 100%, height = 100%, pointerEvents = "none" ]
    ]
